# Caddyfile for the Cloudflare Tunnel box (see nix/nixos/webserver.nix).
# The legacy CentOS server uses ./Caddyfile — do not merge the two.
#
# Cloudflare terminates public TLS at its edge and cloudflared hands plain
# HTTP to Caddy on localhost:80. Every site address is prefixed with http://
# because auto_https off alone does NOT move a bare hostname off port 443 —
# Caddy would still bind 443 and nothing would listen on 80.
#
# Hostnames stay in the addresses so Caddy still vhost-routes on Host.
{
	auto_https off
}


